				<pubDate>Thu, 10 Jul 2025 12:25:06 +0200</pubDate><author>mail@christianmahnke.de (Christian Mahnke)</author>
				<guid>https://backsteinexpressionismus.projektemacher.org/en/post/die-deutsche-zeitung/manifest.json</guid>
				<description>&lt;p&gt;The &#xA;        &#xA;          &#xA;        &lt;a data-wikidata-entity=&#34;Q2108907&#34; href=&#34;https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pressa&#34; target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener noreferrer&#34;&gt;Pressa in Cologne in 1928&lt;/a&gt; has been a topic in this blog before, as some relevant buildings were erected in preparation for it. Here is a publication that appeared as part of the exhibition and presents various German newspapers including their buildings. Not everything is Brick Expressionism.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;On the back of the publication there is a type specimen, which can be found on &lt;a href=&#34;https://schriftmuster.projektemacher.org/post/fette-metropolis&#34; target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener noreferrer&#34;&gt;&amp;ldquo;Schriftmuster&amp;rdquo;&lt;/a&gt; (German).&lt;/p&gt;</description>
